# POLYBOT .env: KEYS AND PASSWORDS ONLY. NEVER commit this file.
#
# Every trading/risk/strategy setting (capital, trade size, daily loss limit, take profit,
# stop loss, rule auto-approval, latency limits ...) lives in the dashboard: Settings page.
# Nothing else needs to be written here.
#
# Uncomment a line only when you give it a real value. Do not leave an empty "KEY=" line and
# do not define a key twice: the last definition wins.

# --- Dashboard login (REQUIRED). Run:  python -m btc5m_bot hash-password
# and paste the two lines it prints here:
# POLYBOT_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH=
# POLYBOT_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Polymarket CLOB API credentials (REQUIRED, even in PAPER: they verify the Chainlink oracle)
# POLYBOT_CLOB_API_KEY=
# POLYBOT_CLOB_API_SECRET=
# POLYBOT_CLOB_API_PASSPHRASE=

# --- Wallet (only for LIVE trading / authenticated exchange access)
# POLYBOT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# POLYBOT_FUNDER_ADDRESS=
# POLYBOT_SIGNATURE_TYPE=0

# --- Database (recommended on hosts without a persistent disk, e.g. Render free)
# One Postgres URL for everything the bot stores: Settings page, orders, positions, paper trades,
# approved rules, risk state, audit log. Unset = local SQLite file + runtime.json.
# (DATABASE_URL is also accepted; POLYBOT_SETTINGS_DATABASE_URL is the old name and still works.)
# POLYBOT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# --- Hosting only (rarely needed; sensible defaults are built in) ---
# Dashboard bind address / port, public health port, data folders, heartbeat (LIVE only) and
# other infrastructure options are optional POLYBOT_* variables: see the README.
